title = Afghan Hound
description = The Afghan Hound (Pashto: تاژي سپی Tāžī Spay Dari: سگ تازی Sag-e Tāzī ) is a hound distinguished by its thick, fine, silky coat, and a tail with a ring curl at the end. The breed originates in the cold mountains of Afghanistan where it has been bred for speed and game hunting. Other names for this breed are Tāzī, Thasi, Barakzai Hound, and Balochi Hound.
